course: dictionary
lesson: 4448
title: Hang: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word hang is a good example. «Hang your coat on the hook» means put it up so it is held from above. In «hang up», it means something else again, so look at the words around it before you choose.
explain: Hang can also describe something held from above with its lower part free. «A spider monkey hangs by its tail alone» shows the monkey holding on from above. «Bats sleep hanging upside down» shows the same idea: held from above, with nothing holding them from below.
explain: Some hang phrases mean something different from the single word. «Hang out with friends» means spend time together doing nothing special. «Hang in there» means do not give up. «Get the hang of» something means learn how to do it. Ask yourself: is something being held up, or is a person doing something?
fact: Hang is a verb with the forms hang, hangs, hung and hanging.
fact: «Hang» can mean to put something up so it is held from above, like a coat on a hook.
fact: «Hang up» can mean to end a phone call, as in «so you don't hang up» (stay on the line).
fact: «Hang out» and «hang around» mean to spend time somewhere doing nothing special.
fact: «Get the hang of» something means to learn how to do it.
exercise: «Hang your coat on the hook.» What does hang mean here? | Wash it carefully | Pull it down hard | Stop it from moving | *Put it up so it is held from above
exercise: «The call handler asks where you are, so you don't hang up.» What does hang up mean? | Stop breathing | Climb up a wall | *End the phone call | Fall asleep
exercise: «Bats sleep hanging upside down.» What is happening to the bats? | They are standing on the ground | They are flying across the sky | *They are held from above, with nothing holding them from below | They are swimming in a cave
test: «Hang in there» means what? | Make a loud noise | Climb the tree | Hang the picture straight | *Do not give up
test: Which phrase means you learn how to do something? | Hang the washing | Hang out | Hang up | *Get the hang of it
exam: Dani says, «Let's hang out at the park.» What does hang out mean? | Hold something up high | End a phone call | Learn to fly | *Spend time there doing nothing special
